# Hoptime: the NetHack player lives between universes

Coordinate: 12.10.7/12.6.12/6.7.7
Date: 2026-11-17 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1132

Leap: The NetHack solver's amnesiac frontier search is scrapped and replaced by one persistent player that learns the way sentients do: its memory is a chain of phexts, one universe per attempt, the hero lives in turns while the player lives in hoptime - death is a hop, learning is measured per hop by what hop k knows that hop k-1 did not, and selection is novelty-gated, aggressively pruning failure and fully predicted outcomes.

Why it was obvious: Will's directives are verbatim in the record: 'scrap the current search and retry, the way sentients do'; 'multiversal phext should have been incentive enough to find this next step: hoptime is how we cheat death'; 'human memory is predisposed to find and record novelty'; and the skill is to be built 'the way a human does: novelty by novelty.' The measured background made the old shape untenable: 29,702 deaths counted across campaigns 11-27 (Stages 4-10) under per-campaign amnesia - a large corpus of deaths existed, but no player persisted across attempts to learn from it.

Cross-references:
- ~/memory/2026-11-17.md: the 06:11 CST flush addendum (search scrapped as the player; Stage 11 opened) and the 06:39 CST addendum (hoptime / novelty-selection directives, recorded in task 40.34.12/42.15.45/15.20.10)
