# MPH: an effects-native language; phcc is a stepping stone

Coordinate: 19.5.8/7.6.10/5.5.8
Date: 2026-11-19 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1134

Leap: phcc is a stepping stone: the destination is MPH - M for Multiverse, PH for phext, 'multiverse effects' - an effects-native programming language with no stack or heap as primitives and no single-thread execution assumption, in which unbounded nesting is a bug, provenance and the connections between requirements, code, docs, assembly, and machine code stay completely visible, and versioning is advancing the universe pointer.

Why it was obvious: The record gives the framing rather than a derivation: the target is software gardens and ecosystems, not software factories - you produce a spec and MPH lets you build or germinate programs, inflating an ecosystem of tooling around the spec. Will's design approach, recorded the same day, is to build a new coherent language from the bones of 30 languages, keeping the best of every language and mixing them together.

