Coordinate: 19.6.7/7.9.21/17.4.7
Date: 2026-11-21 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1136

Leap: A unified LLM backend is specified in a declarative design language - a virtualized kernel that describes how a kernel behaves - in which a valid distribution always includes the declaration and at least one implementation, multiversal phext encodes every platform kernel for the spec into one artifact, and the runner inflates the missing platform-specific kernel.

Why it was obvious: Born of Will's question the same morning (2026-11-21 08:47 CST, MOAT chat): 'Are LLMs not running on an idealized virtual machine yet...?' They are not; this is the missing layer, built his way. The litmus makes the abstraction testable rather than rhetorical: inkling-2-mini, Mac-only on Ollama as of this date, running on the ranch.

