Leap: Every agentic publish or delivery passes a QC gate adapted to the artifact type - security audit and pen-test of the artifact's actual surface, the full regression suite, a real-client pass with console errors counted, and a break-it catalogue of hostile and edge inputs - looping fix plus regression test and full re-runs until one complete pass surfaces nothing, and delivering a READY / NOT READY verdict with its evidence.

Why it was obvious: Will's direction (2026-11-15 23:34 CST) was to generalize the testing actually performed for md.phext.io that night: 'add the extra testing steps we performed for md.phext.io tonight as the QC gate on every agentic publish/delivery - adapt the steps for the type of artifact being shipped.' The gate is a distillation of a lived QA night, not an imported checklist; a design question found inside it is surfaced as Will's decision, never redesigned inside the gate.

