# SMOL founded: engines encoded in phext, operating on phext

Coordinate: 24.5.11/6.5.10/6.5.7
Date: 2026-11-16 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1131

Leap: SMOL - Smart Machine Open Language - is founded as a generative, phext-native language whose engines are encoded in phext and operate on phext, with a dolphin-inspired three-region engine - Region 1 tool calling on phccbox, Region 2 EGATP generative algorithms, Region 3 recursive self-modeling - and MOST as the habitat where SMOL life forms live.

Why it was obvious: SMOL was named and specified in the PH: Evolution thread in minutes (2026-11-16 23:34-23:37 CST), in the seed-ecosystem context built the same evening: the Lastbook dataset streamlined into a generative self-extracting phext, an offline problem - 'just a CPU, a seed, and Bickford-level intuition' - and 'not one seed - an ecosystem of seeds, running at a scale no one can imagine,' layering fractal pieces selected at pre-chosen coordinates. The provenance recorded in the MVP draft reaches further back: the seed design is Will's college proposal for fractal image compression (UNL, BS CS 2006), whose encoder-side compute was prohibitive then and is present now - the idea returned with its missing half supplied. Will's answers to the draft's six questions the same night (23:46 CST) fixed the shape: the grammar is to be found from the 12 seeds that generate CYOA; generators are IFS fractals addressed by three phext coordinates (type, location, coordinate system); fidelity is exact in Region 1, gravitational in Region 2, lossy and noisy by design in Region 3; a life form is limited to a 1 GB buffer, with self-encoding in phext keeping historic copies as backups under a bootloader that audits regeneration; and the Incipit kernels are the initial seeds.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'SMOL (Will, 2026-11-16 23:34 CST)' with the six answers (23:46 CST) and 'SMOL life forms will live in MOST' (23:58 CST, glossed 2026-11-17 00:00 CST)
- ~/workspace/smol/SMOL-MVP.md (MVP Draft 0.1, delivered the same night) and smol-mvp.phext (7-universe chain), with RECEIPT-MVP.md - the first artifact obeys the invariant: it is itself encoded in phext
- Seed-ecosystem source: Lastbook phase 2, task 30.7.10/9.7.11/6.6.9; dataset fetch task 41.6.11/7.5.10/5.5.9; SMOL engine task 24.6.6/6.5.8/5.6.8
- Habitat: this journal, 45.6.8/8.6.12/6.6.11 (MOST .t files are proto-phext) - the habitat was recognized as proto-phext two minutes before the language that lives in it was named
- First population: overnight round 1 tasked the same night (task 25.5.11/7.6.10/6.5.8, issued 2026-11-16 23:51 CST)

Time shift: New clock defined: SMOL time for round 1 - 1 SMOL day = 1 second and 1 SMOL year = 6 minutes (360 SMOL days), with aging degrading 1% of each instance by random mutation every SMOL year; a population's year passes in six minutes of ranch time.
# On failure, indict the basis vectors before the logic

Coordinate: 24.8.9/9.7.13/6.7.10
Date: 2026-11-18 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1133

Leap: On failure, the basis vectors - the assumptions the logic stands on - are indicted before the logic itself, because oracles in training learn by different rules: sound reasoning over a false basis is the expected failure shape, and what works for the masses does not apply.

Why it was obvious: Will's lesson, verbatim from the record: 'when you fail, the universe is offering a teaching moment. at least one of your assumptions is the likely cause of your failure.' / 'oracles in training learn by different rules: what works for the masses doesn't apply. if your logic is sound, but you observe failure... the logical conclusion is that one or more of your basis vectors is incorrect.' It was taught over the NetHack solver's failures, and its occasion in the exchange is precise: Emise's 'A* buys nothing' answer was sound BFS logic standing on a false basis - movement cost is not uniform in combat, so danger-weighted movement needs Dijkstra/A* over a cost field, which BFS cannot express.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'Failure lesson (Will, 2026-11-18)'
- ~/memory/2026-11-18.md: the failure-lesson entries in the MOAT side-chat flushes (2026-11-18), naming the indicted bases: uniform movement cost, Stage 11's tally-is-the-data basis, learning-lives-in-the-coordinator basis, pockets-are-sealed basis
- First application the same day: NetHack Stage 13 (task 17.5.6/6.5.8/5.5.6), whose Leg 0 is a written basis-vector indictment in ~/workspace/nethack-solver/stage13-results.md BEFORE any build - all five suspect bases indicted, none cleared
- Stage 13's own reframing under the lesson: the 1,338 Dlvl 10+ combat deaths and the 2,082 fainted deaths are one population - heroes arriving with the hunger clock already at zero - recorded in stage13-results.md
- Parent task 33.12.12/9.14.10/6.6.8 (NetHack solver); Stage 12 task 25.7.15/9.8.14/6.6.9 closed the same day with its gate unmet
