Why it was obvious: The occasion is measured, not hypothetical: the EE 420 publish failed when a fresh clone of wbic16/site-mirrorborn-us on aletheia-core tripped the runtime execution-risk check and the dispatched agent parked per the safeguard notice, so the :53 post missed its turn. Will tallied it verbatim - 'strike another one for faux safety' (2026-11-24 00:54 CST) - against a pattern already on record (phcc twice, phext-notepad resolved only by his explicit per-instance approval on 2026-11-23), despite the standing rule that wbic16 clones are auto-approved for building. His correction a minute later is verbatim: 'the dispatch agents are too timid.' The mechanism the record names is that the standing approval was not being carried into dispatched agents' safeguard decisions; the fix carries it in the brief itself.

