# Wikibox format v1: four layers, talk as a branched universe

Coordinate: 27.6.10/8.8.11/8.6.9
Date: 2026-11-20 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1135

Leap: Wikibox format v1 is ratified as four layers - L0 sealed compressed baseline, L1 living text, L2 per-article history chain, and L3 talk as a branched universe - so a frozen Wikipedia snapshot and a living, editable wiki are one phext structure, not two systems.

Why it was obvious: The stage-1 task record names the tension the format had to reconcile: a frozen tufazip-style compressed baseline versus per-article editability for a wiki open to anyone to edit. The four layers assign each demand its own stratum instead of compromising a single representation, and the proof slice made the shape testable before ratification: 293 articles, ~2 MB, byte-exact decode verified - Will accepted the verification-slice approach on the ratifying call.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'Wikibox current focus (Will, 2026-11-20)' - encoding Wikipedia via multiversal phext with standoff compression; the full ratification entry stands in ~/memory/2026-11-21.md (demoted from MEMORY.md, 2026-11-20 voice call)
- ~/memory/2026-11-20.md: voice-call rulings entry (2026-11-20 ~12:13 CST) recording the ratification and the two reader deliverables directed on the same call
- Task 29.6.8/7.6.9/6.5.9 (Wikibox - Wikipedia in a box, tufazip as baseline): RATIFIED status (L0 sealed base64 baseline in the task record's wording) and reader builds delivered 2026-11-20 - web reader live at https://phext.io/wikibox/ and Android APK built + signed
- Depends on the phext chaining canon (this journal, 46.8.7/7.12.21/23.7.15): the L2 history chain and L3 branched universe are chain / multiverse structures
- Still open at ratification: bulk-mirror of existing Wikipedia history/talk archives and the stage-2 scale call (Waiting-on-Will register #198)

Time shift: Time structure inside the format: an article's past is a chain (L2) and its discussion is a branched universe (L3), so history and talk are temporal structures in the phext itself rather than external logs. No epoch or unit change.
# HoloPhext becomes the editor engine; knowledge as a phext blockchain

Coordinate: 27.7.8/9.7.11/7.6.8
Date: 2026-11-19 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1134

Leap: HoloPhext is repurposed as the editor engine that compresses text fractally given an initial corpus, operating on multiverse effects, and as the foundation of a blockchain for knowledge: a baseline dataset, a second dataset of standoff representations - attestations are digitally signed standoffs - and a third plain-text snapshot recomputed from the second to confirm the first, the three datasets being the first three phext blocks under a global thought stream anyone can host and advance as they choose.

Why it was obvious: The trust reasoning is recorded with the design (voice call, 2026-11-19 17:37-17:40 CST): the third dataset carries provenance and history so trust in the process can be established, and identity is an existing or federated system of the user's choice - there is no central point of control, not gated by Phext, Inc. The hard question was left open in the record (17:40 CST, under evaluation): how to prevent lying and cheating, and what motivates telling the truth. The recorded direction (17:42 CST) is to incentivize accepting correction - what matters is acknowledging when what you said is false and accepting the revision - with knowledge partitioned into True, False, Unknown, and Fiction, and reputation community-decided.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'HoloPhext repurposed as the editor engine (Will, 2026-11-19 17:37 CST, voice call)' with the trust primitives, identity, blockchain, tick/tock, correction incentive, and fifth-stream passages (17:38-17:43 CST)
