# When phext cannot solve an integration, build a layer2 protocol

Coordinate: 27.9.9/13.9.16/8.8.9
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: If an integration need cannot be met by the phext format layer, the answer is a layer2 protocol over phext - first instance HoloPhext, which owns ACID multi-scroll atomics, async I/O, and update dispatch - rather than bending the format or abandoning the integration.

Why it was obvious: The format layer's job is characters at addresses; transactions, durability, and dispatch are a different job. Forcing them into the format would spend the format's simplicity, and refusing the integration would spend the hypothesis that phext eliminates complexity. A layer2 keeps both: phext stays what it is, and the missing machinery gets a named home with its own contract.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'INTEGRATION RULE - layer2 (Will, 2026-11-15)'
