# Range syntax ratified; phextura is downstream of phext, always

Coordinate: 28.7.7/5.6.6/5.5.10
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: Within-scroll addressing is ratified for libphext v0.6.1: a point is $N:<address>@<line>,<column>, an offset selects forward a counted number of UTF-8 characters to the scroll boundary, ranges are two full points joined by a hyphen and are half-open, columns count Unicode scalar values, the canonical form omits $1: always - and phextura is reformulated to be downstream of phext in every case.

Why it was obvious: Each sub-ruling removes a class of divergence. Half-open ranges compose without off-by-one seams; scalar columns make every one of the nine language ports count the same column on the same text; omitting $1: keeps the common case terse while the parser still accepts it. The downstream ruling is the architectural one: phextura had grown parallel forms duplicating phext concepts, and two grammars for one idea is how the qexo parser episode (this journal, 19.8.8/11.9.13/8.8.10) happens at the format layer.

Cross-references:
- ~/workspace/libphext-ports-v06/RANGE-SYNTAX-PROPOSAL.md (Status: RATIFIED by Will, 2026-11-15; offset form 12:10 CST, open questions ruled one by one 12:30-12:33 CST)
- Register #162 closed on the ratification; follow-on task 20.7.9/9.8.11/8.7.9 (phextura reformulation audit)
- Implementation: all nine libphext ports at parity, 69/69 conformance operations each, fixtures minted from the Rust port; libphext 0.6.1 published to crates.io from the tagged merged tree (2026-11-15)
- Depends on chaining (this journal, 46.8.7/7.12.21/23.7.15) for the $N: universe prefix

